>> title: Full-Sour Dill Pickles
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: cucumber, dill, fermented, pickle, deli
>> counters: Deli
>> aka: sour pickles, sour dills, full sours, dill pickles, fermented pickles, barrel pickles, kosher dills, deli pickles, old pickles
>> pairs-with: deli-rye-bread
>> servings: 12
>> time: 23 days 2 hr
>> slack: unforgiving — anything that sits above the brine goes mouldy and takes the jar with it, so skim the film and keep everything under the surface

>> step: stir the 5% brine
Dissolve @kosher salt{50%g}(3 1/2 Tbs Morton, or 1/3 cup Diamond Crystal; nothing iodised) in @filtered water{4%cup}(950 mL) until the water is clear.

>> step: trim and soak 2 hr
Shave a thin slice off the blossom end of @Kirby cucumbers{2%lb}(900 g) and ~soak{2%hr} in @ice water{2%qt}(2 L).

>> step: pack the jar
Pack @&(~1)cucumbers{} upright into a #half-gallon jar{} with @garlic{6%cloves}(peeled, crushed), @fresh dill{1%bunch}(seed heads and all), @yellow mustard seed{1%Tbs}, @black peppercorns{1%tsp}, @coriander seed{1%tsp}, @bay leaves{2}, @dried red chile{1}, and @grape leaves{2}(or 1 black tea bag), whose tannin holds the crunch.

>> step: cover with brine, ferment 3 weeks at 65-70°F (18-21°C)
Pour @&(~3)brine{} over @&(~1)packed jar{} to cover by an inch, weight everything under the surface, set the lid on loose, and ~ferment{3%weeks} at 65-70°F (18-21°C), until they are sour to the middle.

>> step: chill 2 days
Refrigerate @&(~1)pickles{} ~chill{2%days} before eating; they keep 2 months, going slowly softer.
